From 8930ab700e91e98a5b4ccacdaba35ee0fa1508dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 12:30:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08092/11362] [outer-loop] Masked re-score of 116 induced
 engines: effect survives, tn36 degeneracy is a corpus defect not a mask
 switch

Answers the hud_mask_limitation the object-perception A/B recorded against itself
("both this A/B and the headroom harness construct the verifier bare, so
REQ-ARC-WMTE-6010's compare-time HUD masking is OFF"). Re-scores all 116 committed
engines on the same held-out split through the shipped WorldModelVerifier with
hud_mask supplied and hud_mask_enabled=True, plus the 31 best-of-N candidates that
are the only corpus carrying plan_found.

Q1 the degeneracy does NOT die. On tn36's best-of-N window all 25 changed cells
across all 25 changing transitions lie inside row 1, one per transition -- so the
six perfect-1.0 bar-tickers ARE the bar, and masking it leaves a corpus with zero
dynamics. Both shipped mechanisms refuse that mask (the capture withheld row 1;
REQ-ARC-WMTE-6015's swallow guard refuses it at overlap 1.0000, 25 changing -> 0).
Only a labelled guard bypass yields 0.0, and there the single PLANNABLE candidate
falls to 0.0 too. A corpus defect, not a grading switch.

Q2 the effect SURVIVES: mean per-game delta +0.07402 masked vs +0.07208 unmasked,
+15/-3/=2, p=0.0075378, CI [+0.01336,+0.13277]. But the p gain is a DATA LOSS, not
evidence: s5i5 -- one of the four games that disagreed -- went to exactly 0.0 and
was dropped as a tie. The mean, which keeps ties, moved +0.0019.

Q3 UNESTABLISHED and unimproved by masking: AUC 0.431034 unmasked and identical
under every guard-respecting arm, CI [0.207,0.690] spanning 0.5 at n_plannable=2.
Rank stability answers the same question where n is not 2: Spearman rho 0.978079
over the masked units, 6 inversions in 630.

Activation proven per arm (applied/64 cells on 36 of 116 cells, 24 moved), not
asserted. Unmasked arm reproduces the published primary exactly. Two independent
full runs agree on every arm of all 156 units. adversarial_verify 0-flagged.

Adversarial review of the first build found two real gaps, both now measured and
reported: the only perfect score that was ACTUALLY masked (tn36__r2__on, stays 1.0
with 3 of 4 cells outside the bar) was missing, and 4 of the 7 arms are
byte-identical on the A/B corpus.

