@@ -0,0 +1,3722 @@
+{
+ "experiment": "arc_hud_masked_rescore_20260801",
+ "schema": "carnot.arc.hud_masked_rescore.v1",
+ "title": "Re-score of 116 induced world-model engines with compare-time HUD masking ON, and of the 31 best-of-N candidates that carry plan_found",
+ "run_date": "2026-08-01T16:29:58Z",
+ "git_head": "cde595c970af64a439d1c12e457c4f55a0f13abc",
+ "requirement": "REQ-ARC-WMTE-6010 / 6015 / 6017",
+ "milestone": "outer-loop 2026-08-01",
+ "honest_verdict": "complete_masked_rescore_effect_survives_p_0_0075_but_the_p_gain_is_a_lost_negative_game_not_new_evidence_and_the_tn36_degeneracy_does_not_die_because_the_shipped_guard_refuses_that_mask_and_forcing_it_deletes_the_whole_corpus\n\nTHE HEADLINE, WHICH IS NOT THE ONE THE TASK EXPECTED. Masking does NOT fix the degeneracy, and the reason is not that the mask is wrong -- it is that on tn36's best-of-N window there is nothing else to measure. All 25 changed cells across all 25 changing transitions of that corpus lie inside row 1, one cell per transition. So the six perfect-1.0 bar-tickers are a perfect model of that corpus, the metric was indeed measuring the HUD, and masking the HUD leaves a corpus with zero dynamics. change_fidelity then reads 0.0 for ALL EIGHT tn36 candidates -- including the single PLANNABLE one, which falls from 0.235294 to 0.0 alongside the tickers. The degeneracy dies by the metric becoming undefined, not by the metric becoming discriminating. This is a CORPUS defect, not a masking switch.\n\nAND THE SHIPPED GUARD ALREADY REFUSES IT, CORRECTLY. Two independent shipped mechanisms both decline to apply that mask, neither of which was touched here: the capture artifact WITHHELD tn36 row 1 from the default mask at its stage-2 gate (so the default arm resolves `unresolved` and the six stay at 1.0), and when the withheld band is folded in anyway, REQ-ARC-WMTE-6015's swallow guard refuses it `refused_swallows_dynamics` / `no_changed_cells_outside_mask_cannot_distinguish` at changed_cell_overlap 1.0000, 25 changing transitions -> 0. Only a deliberate, labelled guard bypass produces the 0.0 figures above. The guard is doing exactly the job over-masking asymmetry demands of it.\n\nQ2 SURVIVES, AND ITS APPARENT IMPROVEMENT IS A DATA LOSS. Masked with the shipped default masks: mean per-game delta +0.07402 (unmasked +0.07208), sign test +15/-3/=2, p=0.0075378, bootstrap CI [+0.01336, +0.13277] -- same direction, essentially the same magnitude, CI still excludes 0. But p did NOT fall from 0.0192 to 0.0075 because the evidence got stronger. It fell because s5i5 -- one of the FOUR games that disagreed with the effect -- went from delta -0.030303 to EXACTLY 0.0 and was dropped as a tie, taking the discordant count from 19 to 18. Masking zeroed the single non-zero score s5i5 had (its r0 control cell, 0.090909 -> 0.0), so both arms are all-zero there and the game now contributes nothing at all. Losing a disagreeing game makes the test look better while the evidence base gets smaller. The mean delta, which does not drop ties, moved +0.0019. That is the number to read, and this p should not be quoted without this sentence.\n\nQ3 IS UNESTABLISHED AND MASKING DOES NOT IMPROVE IT. The plannability association is AUC 0.431034 unmasked and 0.431034 under every guard-respecting masked arm -- IDENTICAL, because the default mask reaches only tu93's 5 candidates on that corpus and neither plannable candidate is tu93. CI [0.207, 0.690] spans 0.5 at n_plannable = 2. Under the forced arm it is 0.396552. There is no evidence here that masking makes fidelity rank plannable engines higher, and n=2 could not establish it either way.\n\nONE PERFECT SCORE WAS ACTUALLY MASKED, AND IT SURVIVED. Exactly one of the 116 A/B engines scores a perfect unmasked change_fidelity -- tn36__r2__on -- and on the A/B window the tn36 row-1 mask IS applied. It stays at 1.0: 4 correct changed cells unmasked, 3 masked, i.e. one of its four cells was the bar and it modelled the other three correctly too. So a perfect change_fidelity is NOT by itself the degeneracy. It rests on ONE gradable transition and cannot carry a claim, but it points the opposite way to the best-of-N result and is reported for that reason. The same game yields opposite corpora: 25 of 25 changed cells inside row 1 in the best-of-N window, 12 of 2636 in the A/B window.\n\nMASKING IS REAL AND IT IS SMALL. Proof it activated: hud_mask_status `applied` with hud_mask_cells 64 on 36 of 116 A/B cells (6 of 20 games), and 24 of those 36 changed their change_fidelity. Proof it barely matters: over the masked units Spearman rho between masked and unmasked scores is 0.978079 (6 pairwise inversions in 630), mean absolute shift 0.010190. On the 14 unmasked games the arm is identical to unmasked BY CONSTRUCTION and is labelled so rather than presented as a second measurement.",
