+  "IS_IT_ESTABLISHED": "NO, and it cannot be at this sample size. n_plannable = 2 against 29. The unmasked AUC is 0.431034 with a bootstrap CI of [0.206897, 0.689655], which spans 0.5 -- consistent with no association in either direction. Every guard-respecting masked arm returns the IDENTICAL 0.431034, because the default mask reaches only tu93's 5 candidates on this corpus and neither plannable candidate is a tu93 one. The forced arm gives 0.396552. Nothing here supports 'the masked metric ranks plannable engines higher', and nothing here refutes it.",
+  "why_the_ordinal_ranks_are_reported_tie_aware": "under the forced arm 25 of 31 candidates sit at exactly 0.0, so an ordinal rank among them is decided by sort stability. n_candidates_strictly_above and n_candidates_tied_with_it are the fields any positional claim must be made from; reading 'rank 11/31' as better than 'rank 13/31' there would be reading input order as a result.",
